IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter IX -- LAYER 1, section 251(a) to (e):
-- the merger or consolidation of two or more corporations of this State.
--
-- The source is lines 1058 to 1171 of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code
-- Online made by a converter script. It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N.
-- The rules take the facts of ONE merger or consolidation. Layer 1 takes nobody's side: each rule says what the
-- section requires, permits or decides, and the seat layer (dg6-seat.l4) asks it from the individual's side.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (each is a plain input with a comment, and is listed in NOTES.md):
--   * section 103 (dg1): when an instrument is executed, acknowledged and filed, and when it becomes effective;
--   * section 155 (dg3): fractions of shares.
--
-- READING OF "stockholder": section 114(b)(2) lists sections 251 and 252 among those to which section 114(a)'s reading
-- of "stockholders" as "members" does not apply. So the stockholder rules below are not covered for a nonstock
-- corporation (the vote rule answers NOTHING): see the fork register in NOTES.md.

§ `s 251 -- merger or consolidation of domestic corporations`

§§ `s 251(a) the power to merge or consolidate`

-- src:1061 | (a) Any 2 or more corporations of this State may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations or may consolidate into a new resulting corporation formed by the consolidation, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may be, complying and approved in accordance with this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(a) (src:1061)
DECLARE `s 251 Kind of combination` IS ONE OF
    `a merger into a single surviving corporation`
    `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation`

-- Plain gloss: two or more corporations of this State may combine, either by one of them surviving (a merger) or by
-- forming a new corporation (a consolidation), if the agreement complies with the section and is approved under it.
-- src:1061 | Any 2 or more corporations of this State may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations or may consolidate into a new resulting corporation formed by the consolidation, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may be …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(a) (src:1061)
GIVEN kind                                                 IS A `s 251 Kind of combination`
      `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` IS A NUMBER
      `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement complies with s 251`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 251` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(a) the corporations of this State may merge or consolidate` kind `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations` `the agreement complies with s 251` `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 251` MEANS
        `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` AT LEAST 2
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a merger into a single surviving corporation`       THEN `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations`
         WHEN `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation`   THEN TRUE)
    AND `the agreement complies with s 251`
    AND `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 251`

§§ `s 251(b) the board resolution and the agreement`

-- src:1062 | The board of directors of each corporation which desires to merge or consolidate shall adopt a resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation and declaring its advisability …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b) (src:1062)
GIVEN `the corporation desires to merge or consolidate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(b) the board must adopt a resolution approving an agreement and declaring its advisability` `the corporation desires to merge or consolidate` MEANS
    `the corporation desires to merge or consolidate`

-- src:1062 | The board of directors of each corporation which desires to merge or consolidate shall adopt a resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation and declaring its advisability …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b) (src:1062)
GIVEN `the board adopted a resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board declared the advisability of the agreement`                                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(b) the board has adopted the resolution the subsection requires` `the board adopted a resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation` `the board declared the advisability of the agreement` MEANS
        `the board adopted a resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation`
    AND `the board declared the advisability of the agreement`

-- One field per limb of subsection (b): what the agreement of merger or consolidation states, and how it is signed.
-- A field that a limb makes depend on the kind of combination is read only for that kind (see the rule below).
-- src:1062 | The agreement shall state:
-- src:1063 | (1) The terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation;
-- src:1064 | (2) The mode of carrying the same into effect;
-- src:1065 | In the case of a merger, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation …
-- src:1066 | (4) In the case of a consolidation, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement;
-- src:1067 | The manner, if any, of converting the shares of each of the constituent corporations into shares or other securities of the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation, or of cancelling some or all of such shares, and, if any shares of any of the constituent corporations are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of such shares are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of such shares and the surrender of any certificates evidencing them, which cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity may be in addition to or in lieu of shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation; and
-- src:1068 | Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or of any other corporation or entity the shares, rights or other securities of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for any other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b)(1) to (6) (src:1062-1068)
DECLARE `s 251(b) Agreement of merger or consolidation` HAS
    `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some shares of a constituent corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the manner of converting or cancelling those shares`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `some shares of a constituent corporation are not to remain outstanding`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holders of those shares are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity that the holders are to receive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `that provision is consistent with s 155`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 155 (piece dg3)
    `executed by an authorized person`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `is filed`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103`                                            IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)

-- (b)(1) to (b)(5): the agreement shall state them. (b)(3) is for a merger and (b)(4) for a consolidation.
-- (b)(5) has two statements, each required only where its own situation arises ("the manner, if any"; "if any shares ...
-- are not to remain outstanding"): the second is read as required where the holders are to receive something.
-- src:1062 | The agreement shall state:
-- src:1063 | (1) The terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation;
-- src:1064 | (2) The mode of carrying the same into effect;
-- src:1065 | In the case of a merger, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation …
-- src:1066 | (4) In the case of a consolidation, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement;
-- src:1067 | The manner, if any, of converting the shares of each of the constituent corporations into shares or other securities of the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation, or of cancelling some or all of such shares, and, if any shares of any of the constituent corporations are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of such shares are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of such shares and the surrender of any certificates evidencing them, which cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity may be in addition to or in lieu of shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b)(1) to (5) (src:1062-1067)
GIVEN kind      IS A `s 251 Kind of combination`
      agreement IS A `s 251(b) Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` kind agreement MEANS
        agreement's `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`
    AND agreement's `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a merger into a single surviving corporation`
              THEN agreement's `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is`
         WHEN `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation`
              THEN agreement's `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment`)
    AND (    (NOT agreement's `some shares of a constituent corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or cancelled`)
          OR agreement's `states the manner of converting or cancelling those shares`)
    AND (    (NOT (    agreement's `some shares of a constituent corporation are not to remain outstanding`
                   AND agreement's `the holders of those shares are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity`))
          OR agreement's `states the cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity that the holders are to receive`)

-- (b)(6): other details are permitted; a provision for cash in lieu of fractions must be consistent with section 155.
-- src:1068 | Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or of any other corporation or entity the shares, rights or other securities of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for any other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b)(6) (src:1068)
GIVEN agreement IS A `s 251(b) Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(b)(6) the agreement's provision for cash in lieu of fractions is permitted` agreement MEANS
        (NOT agreement's `contains a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities`)
    OR agreement's `that provision is consistent with s 155`

-- "The agreement so adopted shall be executed by an authorized person, provided that if the agreement is filed, it shall
-- be executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103."
-- src:1069 | The agreement so adopted shall be executed by an authorized person, provided that if the agreement is filed, it shall be executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b) closing paragraph (src:1069)
GIVEN agreement IS A `s 251(b) Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(b) the agreement is executed as the subsection requires` agreement MEANS
        agreement's `executed by an authorized person`
    AND (    (NOT agreement's `is filed`)
          OR agreement's `executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103`)

-- The agreement complies with section 251(b) when it states what (b) requires, is executed as required, and any
-- provision for cash in lieu of fractions is consistent with section 155.
-- src:1062 | The agreement shall state:
-- src:1069 | The agreement so adopted shall be executed by an authorized person, provided that if the agreement is filed, it shall be executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b) (src:1062-1069)
GIVEN kind      IS A `s 251 Kind of combination`
      agreement IS A `s 251(b) Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(b) the agreement complies with the subsection` kind agreement MEANS
        `s 251(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` kind agreement
    AND `s 251(b)(6) the agreement's provision for cash in lieu of fractions is permitted` agreement
    AND `s 251(b) the agreement is executed as the subsection requires` agreement

-- A term may depend on facts outside the agreement only if the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how they operate.
-- src:1069 | Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b) closing paragraph (src:1069)
GIVEN `the agreement clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(b) a term of the agreement may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the term` MEANS
    `the agreement clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the term`

-- "The term "facts," as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a
-- determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation." "includes, but is not limited to" makes the list open:
-- an event, or a determination or action by any person or body (the corporation too), is a fact; for anything else the text does
-- not say, so the rule answers NOTHING (NOTES.md fork register F26). The type is used by the same sentence in sections 252(b),
-- 253(a) and 254(c).
-- src:1069 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b) closing paragraph (src:1069)
DECLARE `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on` IS ONE OF
    `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads`
    `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads`
    `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(b) closing paragraph (src:1069)
GIVEN item IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(b) the item is a fact within the meaning of the closing paragraph` item MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads`                                                         THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes`                          THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 251(c) approval by the stockholders, the certificate, and filing`

-- Plain gloss: the agreement goes to the stockholders at a meeting unless no vote is necessary under (f), (g) or (h).
-- src:1070 | The agreement required by subsection (b) of this section shall be submitted to the stockholders of each constituent corporation at an annual or special meeting for the purpose of acting on the agreement. Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the stockholder’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. The notice shall contain a copy of the agreement or a brief summary thereof. At the meeting, the agreement shall be considered and a vote taken for its adoption or rejection …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
GIVEN `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under s 251(f), (g) or (h)` IS A BOOLEAN -- the rules of dg6-s251f-no-vote and dg6-s251h-tender-offer decide it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(c) the agreement is to be submitted to the stockholders at a meeting` `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under s 251(f), (g) or (h)` MEANS
    NOT `no vote of the stockholders is necessary under s 251(f), (g) or (h)`

-- "at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting": read as inclusive, so notice given on the 20th day before the
-- meeting is in time (keel fork F3; NOTES.md fork register F2).
-- src:1070 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the stockholder’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 251(c) the latest date on which notice of the meeting may be given` `the date of the meeting` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 20) `before` `the date of the meeting`

-- src:1070 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the stockholder’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting`         IS A DATE
      `the date notice was given`       IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(c) notice of the meeting was given in time` `the date of the meeting` `the date notice was given` MEANS
    `the date notice was given` AT MOST (`s 251(c) the latest date on which notice of the meeting may be given` `the date of the meeting`)

-- Whoever holds stock, voting or nonvoting, is a person to whom notice is due; the corporation owes it.
-- src:1070 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the stockholder’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
GIVEN `the person holds stock of the corporation, whether voting or nonvoting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(c) the holder is owed notice of the meeting` `the person holds stock of the corporation, whether voting or nonvoting` MEANS
    `the person holds stock of the corporation, whether voting or nonvoting`

-- src:1070 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the stockholder’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. The notice shall contain a copy of the agreement or a brief summary thereof …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
DECLARE `s 251(c) Notice of the meeting` HAS
    `the date of the meeting`                                                         IS A DATE
    `the date notice was given`                                                       IS A DATE
    `notice was given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the holder's address as it appears on the records of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice contains a copy of the agreement or a brief summary of it`                IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1070 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the stockholder’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. The notice shall contain a copy of the agreement or a brief summary thereof …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 251(c) Notice of the meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(c) the notice of the meeting is due notice` notice MEANS
        `s 251(c) notice of the meeting was given in time` (notice's `the date of the meeting`) (notice's `the date notice was given`)
    AND notice's `notice was given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the holder's address as it appears on the records of the corporation`
    AND notice's `notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting`
    AND notice's `notice contains a copy of the agreement or a brief summary of it`

-- "If a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption of
-- the agreement": more than half of the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote (keel forks F4, F5).
-- NOTHING (not covered) for a nonstock corporation (section 114(b)(2)) and for counts that cannot be a vote.
-- src:1070 | At the meeting, the agreement shall be considered and a vote taken for its adoption or rejection. If a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption of the agreement …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
GIVEN kind                                                          IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement`          IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(c) the stockholders adopted the agreement` kind `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
    THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The certificate of incorporation may require "the vote of a larger portion of the stock ... than is required by this chapter"
-- (section 102(b)(4), src:55: piece dg1). The Law's own requirement in section 251(c) is the majority above; where the certificate
-- requires more, the larger requirement is the input of this rule (NOTES.md fork register F24).
-- src:55 | (4) Provisions requiring for any corporate action, the vote of a larger portion of the stock or of any class or series thereof, or of any other securities having voting power, or a larger number of the directors, than is required by this chapter;
-- src:1070 | If a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption of the agreement …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070); § 102(b)(4) (src:55)
GIVEN kind                                                          IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the vote that the certificate of incorporation requires`     IS A `Vote requirement` -- out of range: section 102(b)(4) (piece dg1)
      `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement`          IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(c) the stockholders adopted the agreement by the vote the certificate of incorporation requires` kind `the vote that the certificate of incorporation requires` `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
    THEN `the vote carries` `the vote that the certificate of incorporation requires` `the number of votes cast in favor of the agreement` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The secretary or assistant secretary certifies the adoption on the agreement, unless a certificate of merger or
-- consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement.
-- src:1070 | that fact shall be certified on the agreement by the secretary or assistant secretary of the corporation, provided that such certification on the agreement shall not be required if a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c) (src:1070)
GIVEN `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote was voted for the adoption of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(c) the secretary or assistant secretary must certify the adoption on the agreement` `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote was voted for the adoption of the agreement` `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement` MEANS
        `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote was voted for the adoption of the agreement`
    AND (NOT `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`)

-- "If the agreement shall be so adopted and certified by each constituent corporation, it shall then be filed and shall
