`s 251(c) the certificate of merger or consolidation states what the subsection requires` kind certificate MEANS
        certificate's `executed in accordance with s 103`
    AND certificate's `states the name and state of incorporation of each of the constituent corporations`
    AND certificate's `states that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent corporations in accordance with s 251`
    AND certificate's `states the name of the surviving or resulting corporation`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a merger into a single surviving corporation`
              THEN certificate's `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is`
         WHEN `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation`
              THEN certificate's `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment to the certificate`)
    AND certificate's `states that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation, with the address`
    AND certificate's `states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished on request and without cost to any stockholder of any constituent corporation`

-- The statement in (c)(7) is what a stockholder of any constituent corporation can hold the surviving or resulting
-- corporation to: a copy of the agreement on request, without cost. The text makes the statement a required content of
-- the certificate; it states no separate duty (NOTES.md fork register F6).
-- src:1077 | (7) That a copy of the agreement of consolidation or merger will be furnished by the surviving or resulting corporation, on request and without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(c)(7) (src:1077)
GIVEN `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of filing the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a stockholder of a constituent corporation`                         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(c)(7) the stockholder may request a copy of the agreement without cost` `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of filing the agreement` `the person is a stockholder of a constituent corporation` MEANS
        `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in lieu of filing the agreement`
    AND `the person is a stockholder of a constituent corporation`

§§ `s 251(d) terminating or amending the agreement before it takes effect`

-- Plain gloss: the board of a constituent corporation may terminate the agreement, even after the stockholders have
-- approved it, but only if the agreement says so and only before it becomes effective.
-- src:1078 | Any agreement of merger or consolidation may contain a provision that at any time prior to the time that the agreement (or a certificate in lieu thereof) filed with the Secretary of State becomes effective in accordance with § 103 of this title, the agreement may be terminated by the board of directors of any constituent corporation notwithstanding approval of the agreement by the stockholders of all or any of the constituent corporations …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(d) (src:1078)
GIVEN `the agreement contains a provision that it may be terminated by the board of directors of a constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) has not yet become effective in accordance with s 103`               IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(d) the board of a constituent corporation may terminate the agreement` `the agreement contains a provision that it may be terminated by the board of directors of a constituent corporation` `the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) has not yet become effective in accordance with s 103` MEANS
        `the agreement contains a provision that it may be terminated by the board of directors of a constituent corporation`
    AND `the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) has not yet become effective in accordance with s 103`

-- "a certificate of termination or merger or consolidation": the text's words (read as "of merger or consolidation":
-- NOTES.md fork register F7). It is owed where the agreement is terminated after filing and before it becomes effective.
-- src:1078 | in the event the agreement of merger or consolidation is terminated after the filing of the agreement (or a certificate in lieu thereof) with the Secretary of State but before the agreement (or a certificate in lieu thereof) has become effective, a certificate of termination or merger or consolidation shall be filed in accordance with § 103 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(d) (src:1078)
GIVEN `the agreement was terminated after it (or a certificate in lieu of it) was filed with the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) has not yet become effective in accordance with s 103`     IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(d) a certificate of termination must be filed` `the agreement was terminated after it (or a certificate in lieu of it) was filed with the Secretary of State` `the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) has not yet become effective in accordance with s 103` MEANS
        `the agreement was terminated after it (or a certificate in lieu of it) was filed with the Secretary of State`
    AND `the agreement (or a certificate in lieu of it) has not yet become effective in accordance with s 103`

-- What an amendment made after a constituent corporation's stockholders adopted the agreement does to that corporation's
-- stock. "such constituent corporation" in limbs (1) and (3) is read as the constituent corporation whose stockholders
-- adopted (NOTES.md fork register F8).
-- src:1078 | Any agreement of merger or consolidation may contain a provision that the boards of directors of the constituent corporations may amend the agreement at any time prior to the time that the agreement (or a certificate in lieu thereof) filed with the Secretary of State becomes effective in accordance with § 103 of this title, provided that an amendment made subsequent to the adoption of the agreement by the stockholders of any constituent corporation shall not (1) alter or change the amount or kind of shares, securities, cash, property and/or rights to be received in exchange for or on conversion of all or any of the shares of any class or series thereof of such constituent corporation, (2) alter or change any term of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation to be effected by the merger or consolidation, or (3) alter or change any of the terms and conditions of the agreement if such alteration or change would adversely affect the holders of any class or series thereof of such constituent corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(d) (src:1078)
DECLARE `s 251(d) Effect of an amendment on one constituent corporation` HAS
    `its stockholders adopted the agreement before the amendment`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amendment alters the amount or kind of shares, securities, cash, property or rights to be received for or on conversion of any of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amendment alters a term or condition of the agreement and adversely affects the holders of a class or series of its stock` IS A BOOLEAN

